.IX Title "Lucy::Object::BitVector 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Object::BitVector 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Object::BitVector \- An array of bits.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 6
\&    my $bit_vec = Lucy::Object::BitVector\->new( capacity => 8 );
\&    my $other   = Lucy::Object::BitVector\->new( capacity => 8 );
\&    $bit_vec\->set($_) for ( 0, 2, 4, 6 );
\&    $other\->set($_)   for ( 1, 3, 5, 7 );
\&    $bit_vec\->or($other);
\&    print "$_\en" for @{ $bit_vec\->to_array };    # prints 0 through 7.
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
BitVector is a growable array of bits.  All bits are initially zero.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 3
\&    my $bit_vec = Lucy::Object::BitVector\->new( 
\&        capacity => $doc_max + 1,   # default 0,
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new BitVector.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBcapacity\fR \- The number of bits that the initial array should be
able to hold.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS get
.IX Subsection "get"
.Vb 1
\&    my $bool = $bit_vector\->get($tick);
.Ve
.PP
Return true if the bit at \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR has been set, false if it
hasn’t (regardless of whether it lies within the bounds of the
object’s capacity).
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBtick\fR \- The requested bit.
.SS set
.IX Subsection "set"
.Vb 1
\&    $bit_vector\->set($tick);
.Ve
.PP
Set the bit at \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR to 1.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBtick\fR \- The bit to be set.
.SS next_hit
.IX Subsection "next_hit"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $bit_vector\->next_hit($tick);
.Ve
.PP
Returns the next set bit equal to or greater than \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR,
or \-1 if no such bit exists.
.SS clear
.IX Subsection "clear"
.Vb 1
\&    $bit_vector\->clear($tick);
.Ve
.PP
Clear the indicated bit. (i.e. set it to 0).
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBtick\fR \- The bit to be cleared.
.SS clear_all
.IX Subsection "clear_all"
.Vb 1
\&    $bit_vector\->clear_all();
.Ve
.PP
Clear all bits.
.SS grow
.IX Subsection "grow"
.Vb 1
\&    $bit_vector\->grow($capacity);
.Ve
.PP
If the BitVector does not already have enough room to hold the
indicated number of bits, allocate more memory so that it can.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBcapacity\fR \- Least number of bits the BitVector should accomodate.
.SS and
.IX Subsection "and"
.Vb 1
\&    $bit_vector\->and($other);
.Ve
.PP
Modify the BitVector so that only bits which remain set are those
which 1) were already set in this BitVector, and 2) were also set in
the other BitVector.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBother\fR \- Another BitVector.
.SS or
.IX Subsection "or"
.Vb 1
\&    $bit_vector\->or($other);
.Ve
.PP
Modify the BitVector, setting all bits which are set in the other
BitVector if they were not already set.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBother\fR \- Another BitVector.
.SS xor
.IX Subsection "xor"
.Vb 1
\&    $bit_vector\->xor($other);
.Ve
.PP
Modify the BitVector, performing an XOR operation against the other.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBother\fR \- Another BitVector.
.SS and_not
.IX Subsection "and_not"
.Vb 1
\&    $bit_vector\->and_not($other);
.Ve
.PP
Modify the BitVector, clearing all bits which are set in the other.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBother\fR \- Another BitVector.
.SS flip
.IX Subsection "flip"
.Vb 1
\&    $bit_vector\->flip($tick);
.Ve
.PP
Invert the value of a bit.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBtick\fR \- The bit to invert.
.SS flip_block
.IX Subsection "flip_block"
.Vb 4
\&    $bit_vector\->flip_block(
\&        offset => $offset,  # required
\&        length => $length,  # required
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Invert each bit within a contiguous block.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBoffset\fR \- Lower bound.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBlength\fR \- The number of bits to flip.
.SS count
.IX Subsection "count"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $bit_vector\->count();
.Ve
.PP
Return a count of the number of set bits.
.SS to_array
.IX Subsection "to_array"
.Vb 1
\&    my $i32_array = $bit_vector\->to_array();
.Ve
.PP
Return an array where each element represents a set bit.
.SS clone
.IX Subsection "clone"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $bit_vector\->clone();
.Ve
.PP
Return a clone of the object.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Object::BitVector isa Clownfish::Obj.
